  "modelingNotes": [
    "40 Wall Street (the Trump Building, former Bank of Manhattan Trust Building) — procedural, CC0-1.0, no textures. bun generators/nyc-40-wall-street.ts",
    "Map frame: x = model east, y = model north (Pine Street; Wall Street is the south front), z up, metres. Placed at bearing 37°, the axis of the tower's walls. Anchor: area centroid of the OSM outline way/278042253.",
    "Evidence",
    "OSM way/278042253 (outline) and its 29 building:part ways, which map the Wall Street wings, the light court on the west side, the stepped north block on Pine Street, the tower's three top stages (212/225/230 m) and the pyramid (way/286057109) and its lantern; plans used as drawn, squared to the 37° axis.",
    "Lidar: USGS 3DEP NY_NewYorkCity, flown 2017, resampled into the model frame (heights above the lowest ground by the outline, on Wall Street). Shaft top 206–216 m, a 224–229 m stage, the pyramid's eaves ~230 m and its lantern to ~275 m; the Wall Street wings 73–80 m either side of a 34 m entrance block; the main base 96–98 m and a 122–130 m ring round the tower; the Pine Street block stepping 109/100/87/74/47 m; a 30 m light court on the west side. These replace OSM's heights where they differ (the lidar sits ~3 m north-east of OSM here, so heights were read by matching edges).",
    "Published: 283 m to the spire, 71 floors, H. Craig Severance with Yasuo Matsui, 1930 (Wikipedia; NYC LPC 1995). Buff limestone and brick; a steep green copper pyramid with dormers, stone gables rising into it at the middle of each face, a lantern and a spire.",
    "Photos (Wikimedia Commons): /tmp/city/nyc/work/nyc-40-wall-street/photos/credits.txt",
    "Estimated: the gables' width and height and the dormer count (photos); the lantern's size (lidar peak, photos); the panel rhythm.",
    "Original procedural model from https://github.com/alexwohlbruck/landmarks (catalog id \"nyc-40-wall-street\", model \"nyc-40-wall-street\"), generated by https://github.com/alexwohlbruck/landmarks/blob/c3921f733df14b41e1f6d15853cce7b343886f17/generators/nyc-40-wall-street.ts. That repository is the editable source; source.blend.gz is the exported mesh imported into Blender for convenience.",
    "Exported for Open Landmarks v1: placement bearing and scale baked in; moving parts frozen in their rest pose; footings and basements below the lowest ground (y = 0) cut away; material colours carried over exactly, as library finishes where they are not standard swatches."
  ],
